  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\nDeveloping a Program of Research in Nursing\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nGrounded in the author's 30 years of experience as a highly esteemed\n\nnurse researcher, the book guides nurses step by step through all aspects of program development.\n\nNumerous examples of various types of nursing research programs provide insight\n\ninto potential research paths, and information from the author's own long-term research on postpartum mood and anxiety disorders is used to illustrate concepts throughout the book. The text also includes suggestions for sustaining a research trajectory and provides detailed strategies for publishing successive studies. With an eye to exploring every possible research avenue, the book addresses interdisciplinary collaborative research and international research collaboration.\n\nKey features:\n\n- and the health sciences - Demonstrates how to use both quantitative and qualitative research methods to\n\n- Provides specific steps for developing a successful research program in nursing\n\n- produce a knowledge-driven research trajectory - Provides time-management strategies for research productivity\n- trajectory - Uses concrete examples of research programs, including the author's own\n- Explains how to plan for sequential studies and sustain a successful research\n- programs on postpartum mood and anxiety disorders\n\nPublication Year\n\n2015\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nEdition\n\n1st Ed.\n\nAuthor/Editor\n\nBeck, Cheryl Tatano\n\nPublisher\n\nSpringer Publishing Company\n\nISBN\n\n978-0-826-12325-1\n\nDoody's Star Rating®\n\nScore: 98\n\nDoody Core Title\n\nScore: 2.6 (Research)\n\nPlatform\n\nOvid\n\nProduct Type\n\nBook\n\nSpeciality\n\nReferences\n\nResearch &amp; Theory\n\nLanguage\n\nEnglish\n\nPages\n\n178\n\nIllustrations\n\n0",
